course: dictionary
lesson: 3024
title: Each and every one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Each» means every single one of a group, taken one by one. «Each person has one life on this earth.» Every person has one life, and nobody else can live it for them. It does not mean one life shared by everybody.
explain: After a price or a number, «each» means for every one. «The bread costs 2 dollars each.» So one loaf costs 2 dollars, and 3 loaves cost 6 dollars. Check it by swapping in one: 2 dollars for one, so 2 dollars each.
explain: «Each other» means one another, as in «They hugged each other.» In chatty speech people often drop «each» and say «one each», «a fiver a head» or «3 quid apiece». In exam writing you may see «per», «apiece» or «respectively» instead.
fact: «Each» means every one of a group, taken one by one.
fact: «Each» can be a determiner («each child»), a pronoun («each of them») or an adverb («they cost 2 dollars each»).
fact: After a price, «each» means for one: «costs 4 each» means 4 for one item.
fact: «Each other» means one another, as in «they hugged each other».
fact: In casual talk «each» is often dropped: «a fiver a head», «3 quid apiece», «one each».
exercise: «Each person has one life on this earth.» What does each mean here? | Some people, maybe a few | Only the people who live on islands | *Every single person, one by one | Only the oldest person
exercise: «The bread costs 2 dollars each.» What does each mean here? | *For one loaf | Only the first loaf in the shop | Free of charge | For all the loaves together
exercise: «They hugged each other.» What does each other mean? | Very quietly | *One another | Each one by itself, alone | Two hugs in different places
test: «Hammerhead sharks have an eye at each end.» In this sentence, each means: | Only one end | Very quickly | *Every end, one by one | At the middle
test: Mum says, «Those apples are a pound each.» Another way to say the same thing in casual talk is: | a pound in total | a pound for lunch | a pound for the whole lot | *a pound a piece
exam: Which exam word could replace each in «Tickets cost 5 dollars each»? | *per ticket | by mistake | after lunch | in the box
